# Shared edge proxy for EVERY app on this droplet.
#
# One Caddy owns :80/:443 for the whole host. Each app contributes a site file
# to sites/ at deploy time (edge.sh writes it from site.caddy.tmpl) and this
# Caddyfile imports them all — so putting a second app on a droplet is a new
# file plus a reload, never a second process fighting for port 443.
#
# Naming a site by its public domain triggers Caddy's automatic HTTPS: it
# obtains + renews a Let's Encrypt cert over HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN. That works once
# the DNSimple A record resolves to this droplet's IP and ports 80/443 are
# reachable (firewall story 2.2). Certs persist in the caddy_data volume, which
# is shared by every app on the host.
#
# The glob matches nothing on a brand-new droplet (before any app has
# deployed); Caddy accepts an import that matches no files, so the edge stack
# starts clean and the first site shows up on the first reload.
import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy
